WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.810
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and I had a chance
to see Edge of Tomorrow earlier this week

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:11.740
so that's why I'm posting this so early. I'm
also working on an Emily Blunt Catwoman video.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.940
But I wanted to post this first so you understand
why her becoming the new Catwoman might be

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.190
a really awesome thing.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:21.000
Because most of you probably haven't seen
the movie I'm going to do a non-spoilery review

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.220
first then I'll let you know when we get to
spoilers in case you want to wait to watch

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.390
that part. If you're just finding me for the
first time, since we're in the middle of the

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:32.189
summer movie season I'm doing reviews of the
stuff I'm really excited about like Fault

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.079
In Our Stars, How To Train Your Dragon and
so on. Be sure to subscribe to get everything

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:39.649
and feel free to suggest movies to me.

00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:42.819
The screening I went to was up at Mann's Chinese
Theater in Hollywood. The really big one where

00:00:42.819 --> 00:00:44.350
they do a lot of movie premiere's. Tom Cruise
surprised everyone at the end and answered

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.239
a bunch of questions. Just the screening itself
was a lot of fun. I posted a bunch of pictures

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:49.679
of it on twitter and instagram.

00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:54.929
The last big Tom Cruise science fiction movie
I saw was Oblivion, which looked amazing,

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:59.069
but didn't really make me cheer out loud at
the end. The director of that movie was the

00:00:59.069 --> 00:01:04.100
guy that did Tron Legacy, this movie is a
whole different team of people with the addition

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:09.219
of Emily Blunt and Bill Paxton. And they made
all the difference. Hail Hydra.

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:15.810
It's like Starship Troopers meets Groundhog
Day. And what do those movies have in common.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.850
They both science fiction and they both do
comedy really well. Which is one of the first

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.890
things I noticed about this movie.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.909
I had a really easy time connecting with the
characters, and the way they play with the

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:32.250
conceit of time is pretty cool. The macguffin,
it's all on the posters. Live Die Repeat.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.250
It's like video game logic. You try a strategy,
get squished and respawn so you can try again.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:42.039
It doesn't get so stuck on the way that whole
thing works that it stops being fun. But I

00:01:42.039 --> 00:01:45.740
could make a whole video about the way that
Respawn Time Travel stuff is used. Because

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.770
it's really fascinating the way they chose
to explain it.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:52.829
Tom Cruise said at that screening that he
didn't even think of it as a movie about an

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:57.439
alien attack, it's like Bill Murray in Groundhog
Day where the whole movie revolves around

00:01:57.439 --> 00:02:00.590
his perspective as it changes with each respawn.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:06.210
Emily Blunt also became my new number one
badass movie female of the summer. Lady Brienne

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:11.500
will always rule the bear pit on my TV. But
Blunt works so well in this time loop. Tom

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.800
Cruise is the one who changes a lot each time,
so it creates a lot of opportunities to use

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.410
those respawns for comedy.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:25.410
But the setup for her character is so great,
it reminded me of the first time Woody learned

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.750
about Buzz Lightyear. Tom Cruise being Woody.
Her face is on everything and she's like the

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:35.070
most elite of the elite. Which makes the respawn
jokes so much funnier.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.350
I feel like the humor is really what's going
to make the movie fun to watch more than once.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.540
And there aren't a lot of movies I watch twice
anymore.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.760
The only other non-spoilery thing that I want
to mention is Bill Paxton. This year has been

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.870
good to him. First he literally killed it
on Agents of SHIELD, Hail Hydra. In this movie

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:55.690
he's the character that conveys the entire
narrative. Like the speech or turn of phrase

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.480
that might not seem super important at first,
but then later ends up being what the whole

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:00.850
movie was about.

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:06.770
So when you go see the movie, pay very careful
attention to what Bill Paxton says. He's also

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:12.280
really funny too. As expected. Don't be surprised
if you get flashes of his Hudson character

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:12.990
from Aliens.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:17.450
The only thing I would have liked to see was
more backstory for Emily Blunt's character.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:21.790
We learn a lot about her, but because this
is a Tom Cruise movie, the vast majority of

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:25.370
camera time is spent on him. She does get
some pretty awesome scenes though.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:30.610
So time for my Top 5 moments. So here's where
we get into spoilers so careful if you haven't

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:35.070
seen it yet. But here we got Number 5 - Asshole
Tom Cruise

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:38.790
I'm talking about the beginning of the movie,
before he's sucked into the Time Loop and

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:42.760
starts the Joseph Campbell hero's journey.
If you've never heard about it it's just a

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:47.570
narrative structure that all major Hero stories
share in common. So whenever big budget movies

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:52.230
are made, they stick to all the different
stages in this picture.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:56.680
Asshole Tom Cruise versus the general was
just funny enough that I didn't hate his character

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.870
and watching him get his ass handed to him
that whole first loop was a lot of fun.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.310
Number 4 - Just the editing in general

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:10.180
I loved the way they would hard cut to make
things funnier. They really only used it each

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:14.040
time he died. Each new time it happened, the
slam to him waking up on the pallet got just

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.570
a little bit funnier.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:19.989
Usually editing isn't something you're supposed
to notice. Like the better an editor is, the

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:24.690
less you think about the transitions between
scenes. I think they did a good job of subverting

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.210
that with the respawns.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.790
Number 3 - Buzz Lightyear Emily Blunt

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:34.260
Just to be clear, Buzz Lightyear is funny
because he's kind of an idiot. I'm talking

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:39.420
about that very first time we the audience
meet her. Her face is on all the billboards

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:44.790
and the news casters all talk about her like
she's so amazing the army has made her their

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.130
public face. She's like the biggest badass
ever.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:52.110
Even when Tom Cruise starts to get better,
he's still not as good of a fighter as she

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:56.380
is. So in a real way, she's the biggest badass
of the Summer, which is a lot of vindication.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.090
She's missed out on being in a ton of huge
badass movie roles.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:05.290
I'll talk about it more in my Batman vs Superman
video tonight, but she was originally supposed

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.250
to be Black Widow in Iron Man 2 and she was
supposed to be Catwoman in Christopher Nolan's

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.790
Dark Knight Returns. But it just didn't happen,
so finally she gets the chance to be that

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:19.440
Buzz Lightyear character. Minus the part about
him being really dumb.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.410
Number 2 - Asshole Tom Cruise becomes Badass
Tom Cruise

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:28.350
The hero montage was just as much fun as the
funny montages. And a lot of times those two

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:33.980
things became the same thing. Like Emily Blunt
forcing constant respawns by shooting him

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:34.580
in the head.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.490
I think my favorite badass time loop was the
last one they did on the beach. When he's

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:42.450
doing cartwheels and jumping around Bill Paxton
and the other J Company people and they just

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.850
sit there with their jaws open in disbelief.

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:45.780
What was his name again?

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:51.420
And my number 1 favorite thing about the movie
is Tom Cruise as Kenny from South Park.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:55.920
They don't ever explicitly say how many times
he's died, Emily Blunt only made it to about

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:01.740
300. But I think he died way more. And after
about the first 30 minutes of the movie he

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:07.200
turns into Kenny from South Park and you start
laughing each time he dies.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:11.050
That's really what's going to make this a
fun movie to watch again. For example, Groundhog

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:15.710
Day is one of the most re-played movies in
history. It's constantly on television somewhere.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:19.230
That movie's great for a lot of other reasons,
but I such a nerd for comedy I always get

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:22.970
really excited when a science fiction movie
that's as dark as this can make me laugh a

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:23.210
lot.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:28.850
So now it's your turn. Let me know what your
favorite part was? All the respawns or one

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.510
of the characters?

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:37.510
My biggest question after it all is does Tom
Cruise now have mega time travel powers. Like

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:43.380
he got Alpha Blood and was able to control
resets for the very specific time point. Then

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.570
at the end he got the Omega's blood and was
able to go back even further in time.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:52.010
I think the explanation is that the organism
was like the time machine and the blood was

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:57.949
like the key. So because the Omega died, Tom
Cruise won't be able to respawn anymore.

00:06:57.949 --> 00:07:00.860
Before they explained the time travel stuff
I thought that the General or some other person

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:05.740
was spying for the aliens.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:09.389
But, as I mentioned about Emily Blunt. She
was supposed to be a bunch of big action hero

00:07:09.389 --> 00:07:14.190
characters and it never worked out. Now she's
in talks to be the new Catwoman in Zack Snyders

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:16.240
Batman vs Superman movie. Obviously that would
go on to Justice League etcetera.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.280
I'll be posting that video tonight explaining
the whole situation. Be sure to subscribe

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:23.120
to get it. I'm also seeing Fault in Our Stars
tonight. So that review will probably post

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:23.320
Friday.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:29.570
Right now click here for my big Star Wars
Episode 7 update and click here for my Maleficent

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:33.060
Review. Spoiler Alert Angelina Jolie was amazing.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:39.070
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.
High fives!

